- Custom ORM (DatabaseManagement)
  - General (✓)
   - It needs a persistent space, to save the changed entities. (✓)
   - A flush function to save the changed entities to the database. (✓)
    - Kernel.terminate Subscriber to flush all changes. (✓)

  - Database connection system. (✓)
   - Create a Connection to the database. (PDO or look for the method used in shopware in their DAL) (✓)

  - Possibility to create tables (entities).
   - Entity
    - A Entity needs a Entity class, that is to store the property data. (✓)
     - Should have a function to return the EntityDefinition class. (✓)

    - The EntityDefinition is to define the properties, to make the programming of the schema creation easier. (✓)

    - The EntityCollection is a collection of the entity, that just contain already fetched Entities that will be the response of the EntityRepository search() function. (✓)
     - search() function (✓)
     - searchId() function (✓)

    - Also there needs to be a EntityRepository, but that will be created automatically, that is just for the database connection. (✓)
     - Entity-Registration (✓)
     - query functionalities. (✓)
      - load static values (✓)
      - load relation values (✓)
       - create an entity instance and check if there is already an existing instance (✓)
       - load one-to-one (✓)
       - load many-to-one (✓)
       - load many-to-many (✓)
       - load one-to-many (✓)

    - Create functionality (✓)
     - Entity Table create (✓)
     - Entity write (✓)
    - Update functionality
     - Entity Table update
     - Entity update (✓)
    - Delete functionality
     - Entity Table delete
     - Entity delete (✓)

   - Create a command to generate the database schema.
   - Create a command to import the database schema.

  - Possibility to create properties in the tables (entities), for example a string property with the name "name". (✓)
   - They can also have Flags, like Nullable, OnDelete, Length, ... (✓)

  - Possibility to create relations between properties (✓)
   - OneToOne relation (✓)
   - ManyToOne relation (✓)
   - OneToMany relation (✓)
   - ManyToMany relation (✓)